---
import Base from '../../../../layouts/Base.astro';

const SITE = 'https://precisionsolutionstech.com';
const title = 'TrailSift for iPhone & iPad Support | Precision Solutions Tech';
const description =
  'Support for TrailSift on iPhone and iPad: opening an SD card, card readers, clearing the card, the lens check, wind and weather, restoring purchases, and common questions.';

const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'iOS Apps', item: `${SITE}/ios-apps/` },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'TrailSift', item: `${SITE}/ios-apps/trailsift/` },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: 'Support', item: `${SITE}/ios-apps/trailsift/support/` },
    ],
  },
];
---

<Base title={title} description={description} path="/ios-apps/trailsift/support/" jsonLd={jsonLd} active="ios-apps">
  <div class="wrap">
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <ol>
        <li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
        <li><a href="/ios-apps/">iOS Apps</a></li>
        <li><a href="/ios-apps/trailsift/">TrailSift</a></li>
        <li>Support</li>
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <article class="prose">
      <h1>TrailSift for iPhone &amp; iPad Support</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Something not working, or a question the app does not answer? Email
        <a href="mailto:support@precisionsolutionstech.com">support@precisionsolutionstech.com</a>
        and tell us your device, iOS version, your trail camera model, and what you expected to happen.
        We read every message.
      </p>

      <h2 id="requirements">Requirements</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>iPhone or iPad with iOS / iPadOS 17 or later</li>
        <li>An SD card reader that fits your device: Lightning or USB-C</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="open-card">Opening a card</h2>
      <p>
        Plug the reader with the card into your iPhone or iPad, open TrailSift and tap
        <strong>Open SD Card</strong>. In the Files window, pick the card (it often shows as
        <strong>NO NAME</strong> or <strong>Untitled</strong>) and tap <strong>Open</strong>. Any folder
        works too: one you copied to iCloud Drive, On My iPhone, or a USB stick.
      </p>
      <p>
        No card handy? Tap <strong>Try the sample card</strong> to see a full scan on real trail camera
        photos.
      </p>

      <h2 id="scan">Scanning</h2>
      <p>
        Keep TrailSift open while it scans; the screen stays on. If the scan is interrupted, open the
        same card again and it picks up where it left off. <strong>Strict</strong>, <strong>Balanced</strong>
        and <strong>Keep more</strong> change how sure TrailSift must be before it keeps a frame. Check
        the <strong>Empty</strong> tab before importing if you want to see what was set aside.
      </p>

      <h2 id="clear-card">Clearing the card</h2>
      <p>
        After an import, TrailSift copies every keeper and checks each copy byte for byte. Only if
        every copy checks out does it offer to clear the card, and only when you confirm. If it says
        the card is locked, slide the small lock switch on the side of the SD card up and try again.
      </p>

      <h2 id="lens-check">“Blurry photos: check the lens”</h2>
      <p>
        TrailSift compares each card with that camera’s usual sharpness, day and night separately.
        When the photos turn blurry partway through, it tells you when it started. Usually it’s fog or
        condensation on the lens, a spider web, a twig or grass in front of the camera, or the camera
        was bumped. Once it’s fixed, tap <strong>Lens is clean now</strong> on the camera’s page. A
        camera’s very first card can’t be judged yet, because there is nothing to compare it with.
      </p>

      <h2 id="weather">Wind and weather</h2>
      <p>
        Wind and weather come from Apple Weather and need a signal and a spot for the camera. Set the
        spot on the camera’s page (<strong>Cards → Cameras</strong>), from the GPS some cameras write
        into their photos, or with <strong>Use my current location</strong> while you stand at the
        camera. Weather history goes back to August 2021. Turn it off any time in Settings.
      </p>

      <h2 id="purchase">Purchase and restore</h2>
      <p>
        Your first card is free, with every feature. After that, a one-time purchase in the app
        unlocks unlimited cards. It is not a subscription.
      </p>
      <p>
        On a new device or after reinstalling, open <strong>Settings</strong> and tap
        <strong>Restore purchase</strong>. Purchases are tied to your Apple Account. Refunds are handled
        by Apple at <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com" rel="noopener">reportaproblem.apple.com</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 id="questions">Common questions</h2>
      <h3>Why does a video say it can’t be played?</h3>
      <p>
        Some cameras record AVI video, which iPhone can’t decode. TrailSift keeps those files and flags
        them so nothing is lost; share them to a computer to watch.
      </p>
      <h3>The animal name is wrong. Can I fix it?</h3>
      <p>
        Yes. Open the photo, tap <strong>Tag</strong> and pick the right animal. Your choice always wins
        over TrailSift’s guess. Check that the camera’s location is right, too: it decides which animals
        are possible.
      </p>
      <h3>Where are my photos kept?</h3>
      <p>
        In TrailSift on your device, included in your iPhone or iPad backups. Save them to the Photos
        app (one album per camera) or share them any time.
      </p>
      <h3>Does TrailSift upload my photos?</h3>
      <p>
        No. Everything runs on your device. See the
        <a href="/legal/privacy/trailsift-ios/">privacy policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
      <p>
        <a href="mailto:support@precisionsolutionstech.com">support@precisionsolutionstech.com</a>
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/ios-apps/trailsift/">TrailSift for iPhone &amp; iPad</a>
        ·
        <a href="/legal/privacy/trailsift-ios/">Privacy Policy</a>
        ·
        <a href="/about/">About us</a>
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>
